15/15 passed. Here's a summary of the fixes:

**`src/auth.py`**
- `has_permission`: was doing case-sensitive `required in user_roles`; changed to compare lowercased roles.
- `is_admin_or_owner`: was using `and` (requiring both admin *and* owner); changed to `or` (either admin or owner).

**`src/inventory.py`**
- `__init__`: mutable default arg `{}` shared state between instances; changed to `None` + `dict(initial)` copy.
- `add`: was overwriting `_stock[sku] = qty` instead of accumulating; changed to `get(sku, 0) + qty`.
- `reserve`: was using `qty >= available` (raising when qty equals available); changed to `>` so exact-stock reservations succeed.
- `release`: was allowing negative reserved counts; added a guard to raise `ValueError` when releasing more than reserved.

**`src/text_utils.py`**
- `slugify`: was not lowercasing alphanumeric chars (only collapsing `--` once); added `.lower()` on input and looped the collapse until no `--` remain.
- `truncate`: was returning `text[:max_len] + suffix` which exceeds max_len; changed to `text[:max_len - len(suffix)] + suffix`.
